From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntoskrnl: MmLockPagableDataSection, IoBuildPartialMdl, IoOpenDeviceInterfaceRegistryKey

Spec stubs before, imported by a driver bundled with UltiMaker Cura: its first call killed the winedevice.exe and every driver in it. MmLockPagableDataSection (MmLockPagableCodeSection is a macro for it) returns a handle -- nothing pages a driver's sections out here, so they are resident and MmLockPagableSectionByHandle / MmUnlockPagableImageSection (FIXME stubs) are right to do nothing. IoBuildPartialMdl describes part of the source MDL's buffer (Length 0: to its end) with the source's pages, locked, nonpaged and I/O-space flags, MDL_PARTIAL, and the source's system address (MDL_PARTIAL_HAS_BEEN_MAPPED when the source was mapped). IoOpenDeviceInterfaceRegistryKey opens, creating it, the Device Parameters key of a registered interface (STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND otherwise); the interface key's path is now made in one place, shared with IoSetDeviceInterfaceState. KefAcquireSpinLockAtDpcLevel / KefReleaseSpinLockFromDpcLevel stay stubs: they are x86-only and SG's WoW64 loads no 32-bit drivers. wdm.h gains the prototypes.
